---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for VixenBliss Agency, covering site data, service providers, cookies, user rights, and contact options."
>
  <p>
    VixenBliss Agency is a creative technology platform focused on AI-assisted visual content, digital storytelling,
    and modern media experiences. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle limited information when visitors browse
    the website, interact with public pages, or contact us by email.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our goal is to keep data practices simple, transparent, and proportionate to the website experience. We do not ask
    visitors to create an account to browse the site, and we aim to collect only the information needed to operate,
    secure, and improve the public experience.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    When you visit the website, some technical information may be processed automatically by the site infrastructure.
    This may include browser type, device type, operating system, language setting, approximate region, referring page,
    timestamps, and basic network information such as IP address.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may also collect interaction information related to how the public site is used. This can include page views,
    navigation events, video loading activity, link selections, scroll behavior, error states, and performance signals.
    This information helps us understand whether the site is loading correctly and whether visitors can move through
    pages without friction.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you contact us directly, we may receive the information you choose to include in your message, such as your name,
    email address, company name, inquiry type, and the content of your request. Please avoid sending information that is
    not relevant to your inquiry.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
  <p>
    We use limited site information to provide, maintain, and improve the website. This includes delivering visual media,
    diagnosing technical issues, protecting the service from misuse, improving loading speed, and making public pages
    easier to read across mobile and desktop devices.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contact information is used to respond to inquiries, support requests, legal questions, partnership discussions, or
    business communications. We may also use aggregated, non-identifying information to understand general campaign
    quality, page performance, and content presentation.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing With Third Parties</h2>
  <p>
    We may work with trusted service providers that help us operate the website. These providers process technical
    information only as needed to deliver their services, maintain reliability, and support the public user experience.
  </p>
  <p>
    Bunny may be used for video hosting, streaming, content delivery, and related performance functions. Directus may be
    used as a content management system to organize and publish site content. Hosting, infrastructure, email, and
    security providers may also process limited technical or communication data in the normal course of operating the
    website.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information. We may disclose information if required by law, to protect the integrity of the
    website, to respond to lawful requests, or to address misuse, security, or operational issues.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
  <p>
    The website may use cookies, local storage, server logs, or similar browser technologies for technical operation,
    performance, security, and basic preference handling. These technologies can help pages load consistently, support
    media playback, remember simple settings, and understand aggregate site behavior.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can manage cookies through your browser settings. Some technical features may work differently if cookies or
    browser storage are disabled. More detail is available in our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
  <p>
    The website may include links to third-party websites, platforms, or services. Those websites are operated by their
    own owners and are governed by their own privacy policies, terms, and security practices. We encourage visitors to
    review those policies before sharing information with external services.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organizational practices designed to protect the website and the limited information
    processed through it. These practices may include access controls, secure provider configuration, monitoring, and
    routine maintenance.
  </p>
  <p>
    No website or online service can guarantee absolute security. We keep our approach practical and focused on reducing
    risk while maintaining a fast, accessible public experience.
  </p>

  <h2>User Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability,
    or objection regarding personal information associated with you. You may also have the right to withdraw consent
    where processing is based on consent.
  </p>
  <p>
    To make a privacy request, contact us using the email below. We may need to verify the request before taking action,
    especially when a request concerns communication records or information connected to a specific email address.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy as the website, providers, or operational needs evolve. When we make changes, we
    will update the date shown on this page. Continued use of the website after an update means the current version
    applies to your visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy inquiries, data requests, support questions, or legal communications, contact
    <a href="mailto:support@vixenbliss.com">support@vixenbliss.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
